%9Setting:%9

    window_close_disconnects (boolean; default: ON)

%9Description:%9

    Disconnects a server when /WINDOW CLOSE closes the last window that
    shows it, so a connection you can no longer see is not left open.

    A server is shown by its network window (named after the server tag),
    any window whose server is sticky to it, a window with a channel or a
    query of it, a window kept for one of its channels (waiting to rejoin
    after a reconnect), and a status window whose active server it is. As
    long as one of them is left, the server stays connected: closing the
    network window while its channels are open in other windows changes
    nothing.

    The server quits with quit_message, as with /DISCONNECT, and a pending
    reconnect of it is dropped. One line in the window that becomes active
    says so. A later /CONNECT gets the server's tag again, not the tag with
    a number appended.

    With the setting OFF a closed window leaves its server connected, as in
    irssi: the connection goes on without a window, and the next /CONNECT
    to the same network opens a second one with a tag such as IRCnet2.

    Only /WINDOW CLOSE does this: a window closed by /PART or by a query
    ending, /DISCONNECT, /QUIT, /UPGRADE and a lost connection work as
    before.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET window_close_disconnects on
    /SET window_close_disconnects off

%9See also:%9

    SET, WINDOW, CONNECT, DISCONNECT, RMRECONNS, QUIT_MESSAGE

